  "releaseNotes": "# AgentOS Core 2.0.0-beta.68\n\n- Adds permanent Agent deletion with durable cleanup plans and safe retries; IDs can be reused only after complete cleanup\n- Removes deleted Agents from API and Token candidates, and prevents old files, grants, callbacks and queued operations from reaching a recreated Agent\n- Provides explicit cleanup for legacy soft-deleted records; installation never automatically deletes historical Agent data\n- Coordinates sandbox maintenance, API configuration and shutdown with deletion, while preserving shared models, SQL, MCP and global Skills\n- Falls back to GitHub's official release-asset API when direct downloads fail, retaining signed manifests, checksums and safe resumable installer downloads\n- Supports an optional persistent Cube IPv4/CIDR egress allowlist for new sandboxes, with empty-list parsing corrected and existing network configuration retained\n- Reuses AgentOS Runtime 1.0.0-beta.28; no template rebuild is required\n\nSource: `346f2e1d1e410ba549a497b6e92400150f21a9be`\n\nCore: macOS arm64, Linux x64 and Linux arm64 (GLIBC 2.28+)\n\nThis is a beta release",
